R:instrumental
S:Clip 17 of a Dust-to-Digital Instagram post (19 October 2026), via the player's Facebook page; draft transcription by machine, from the recording
N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): the clip's sustained part (harmonic/percussive separation) was factored into 18 spectra; 13 were single stones (C sharp 5, E5, F sharp 5, G sharp 5, A5, B5, C sharp 6, D6, E6, F sharp 6, a stone near B6) or their upper partials (the components at C7, D7, E7, F7 and A sharp 6 rise and fall with A5, C sharp 6, B5, C sharp 5 and F sharp 5, and are read as those stones), and three were noise. Strokes were found by spectral flux in the full mix and set on a 0.441 s beat from 0.36 s; the tune's two passes (12.5 s and 28.6 s) agree in 45 of their 56 eighths, bars 2 to 4 exactly; they differ in the first bar (the second pass starts an eighth later) and in the last two (the first leads into the link, the second into the closing section).
N:INTONATION: the low stones are close to equal temperament (C sharp 5 -9, E5 -4, F sharp 5 -10, G sharp 5 -7, A5 -1, B5 -5, C sharp 6 -10 cents); the high ones less so (E6 -20, the B6 stone -22).
N:UNCERTAIN: the high B (b') where it sounds with F sharp: it may be the F sharp stone's overtone, not a second stroke; the strokes marked "?" by the reader (written as the note before, held); the first pass of the tune runs one eighth ahead of the grid (the bar before it is written in 7/8, and the link after it in 9/8); the D6 in the closing section (one stone, struck three times).
M:4/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=136
K:A
